module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.ProjBaseChangeTwist

/-!
# Tag 01N2 in one statement

Let `A` be a graded `R`-algebra with grading `𝒜 : ℕ → Submodule R A`, let `S` be an `R`-algebra,
write `X = Proj 𝒜` and `Y = Proj (S ⊗[R] 𝒜)`, and let `ψ : 𝒜 → S ⊗[R] 𝒜` be the base-change
homomorphism `a ↦ 1 ⊗ₜ a`. Tag 01N2 makes three assertions about the data `(U, r, θ)` attached
to `ψ`: the domain of definition `U(ψ)` is all of `Y`, the square formed by `r_ψ : Y ⟶ X` and
the structure morphisms to `Spec S` and `Spec R` is a fibre product, and the comparison maps
`θ : r_ψ^* 𝒪_X(n) ⟶ 𝒪_Y(n)` are isomorphisms.

Each of the three is established separately —
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjShared.mapDomain_baseChange`,
`Stacks.ProjBaseChange.isPullback_map_Spec` and
`Stacks.ProjBaseChange.isIso_twistMap_includeRight` — and this file states all three together,
so that a single declaration says what the tag says.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ProjBaseChange.mapDomain_isPullback_isIso_twistMap_baseChange`: **the three assertions
  of Tag 01N2 in one statement.**

## Implementation notes

The source's standing hypothesis is a ring map `R → A₀`, a ring map `R → R'` and an
identification `B = R' ⊗_R A`; here `R'` is the `R`-algebra `S`, the ring map `R → 𝒜 0` is the
structure map of the degree-zero part of the graded `R`-algebra, and `B` is the tensor product
`S ⊗[R] A` itself with its base-changed grading `Stacks.ProjBaseChange.grading`. Taking `B` to
be the tensor product is what makes the identification hold by construction, so the three
conjuncts speak about one and the same homomorphism
`Stacks.ProjBaseChange.includeRight`: the morphism of the second conjunct is
`Stacks.ProjBaseChange.map`, which is `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map` of that homomorphism, and the
comparison maps of the third conjunct are its.

`Stacks.ProjBaseChange.isPullback_map_of_baseChange` is the same fibre-product square for a
graded ring `ℬ` only isomorphic to `S ⊗[R] 𝒜`, the identification being given there by an
explicit graded isomorphism; its statement is about `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map` of a homomorphism
`f : 𝒜 →+*ᵍ ℬ` that factors through the base change, which the first and third conjuncts here
are not, so the fibre-product square is taken at the tensor product.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01MY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01MY)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Limits AlgebraicGeometry TensorProduct HomogeneousIdeal
open HomogeneousLocalization Graded CommRingCat
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjShared

universe u

namespace Stacks.ProjBaseChange

variable {R A : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing A] [Algebra R A]
  (𝒜 : ℕ → Submodule R A) [GradedAlgebra 𝒜] (S : Type u) [CommRing S] [Algebra R S]

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 01N2].** Let `A` be a graded `R`-algebra with grading `𝒜`, let `S` be an
`R`-algebra, write `X = Proj 𝒜` and `Y = Proj (S ⊗[R] 𝒜)`, and let `ψ : a ↦ 1 ⊗ₜ a` be the
base-change homomorphism of graded rings. Then `U(ψ) = Y`, the square

```
Y = Proj (S ⊗[R] 𝒜) ⟶ Proj 𝒜 = X
         |                 |
         v                 v
      Spec S      ⟶     Spec R
```

is a fibre product, and every comparison map `θ : r_ψ^* 𝒪_X(n) ⟶ 𝒪_Y(n)` is an isomorphism.

The three conjuncts are, in order:

1. **The domain of definition is everything.** The base-changed irrelevant ideal is generated by
  the images of the homogeneous elements of positive degree, so already the standard opens
  `D₊(1 ⊗ₜ f)` cover `Y`. This is
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjShared.mapDomain_baseChange`.
2. **The square is a fibre product.** The structure morphism of each projective spectrum is
  written as its morphism to the spectrum of the degree-zero part of its grading followed by the
  spectrum of the structure map of that degree-zero part. This is
  `Stacks.ProjBaseChange.isPullback_map_Spec`.
3. **The comparison maps are isomorphisms.** For every `n : ℤ`, the canonical comparison on the
  `n`-th twist along `r_ψ = AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map ψ` is an isomorphism. This is
  `Stacks.ProjBaseChange.isIso_twistMap_includeRight`.

The source's data are the graded `R`-algebra and the `R`-algebra `S`, and those are the only
binders here; the identification of the target graded ring with the base change holds by
construction, since the target is the base change. -/
@[stacks 01N2 "the tag's three assertions in one statement, for the base change of a graded
`R`-algebra `A` along an `R`-algebra `S`: the domain of definition of the base-change
homomorphism is the whole of `Proj (S ⊗[R] A)`, the square it forms with the structure morphisms
to `Spec S` and `Spec R` is a fibre product, and the comparison map on every twist is an
isomorphism"]
theorem mapDomain_isPullback_isIso_twistMap_baseChange :
    mapDomain 𝒜 (grading 𝒜 S) (includeRight 𝒜 S) = ⊤ ∧
      IsPullback (map 𝒜 S)
          (Proj.toSpecZero (grading 𝒜 S) ≫ Spec.map (ofHom (algebraMap S ↥(grading 𝒜 S 0))))
          (Proj.toSpecZero 𝒜 ≫ Spec.map (ofHom (algebraMap R ↥(𝒜 0))))
          (Spec.map (ofHom (algebraMap R S))) ∧
      ∀ n : ℤ, IsIso (Stacks.ProjTwistComparison.twistMap (includeRight 𝒜 S)
        (irrelevant_le_map 𝒜 S) n) :=
  ⟨mapDomain_baseChange 𝒜 (includeRight 𝒜 S) fun _ => rfl, isPullback_map_Spec 𝒜 S,
    fun n => isIso_twistMap_includeRight 𝒜 S n⟩

end Stacks.ProjBaseChange

end
